<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - DLJ, Salomon.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - DLJ, Salomon.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Brown Brothers Harriman &amp; Co said shares of Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette and Salomon Inc have rallied on &quot;unfounded speculation&quot; since the news of the Morgan Stanley-Dean Witter merger.</p>
<p>-- said DLJ and Salomon holders should &quot;consider taking profits&quot; following the recent run-up in share price.</p>
<p>-- said neither DLJ or Salomon is likely to follow in Morgan Stanley's footsteps in the near future.</p>
<p>-- said Salomon already has an alliance with Fidelity Investments. Any moves by Salomon into the retail business are not likely to occur for at least a year, Brown Brothers said.</p>
<p>-- said DLJ already has built-in retail distribution capacity through its Pershing correspondent network of region brokerage firms.</p>
</text>
